From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] linux: never build the jni FFI plugin into the desktop bundle

Class:   LOCAL WORKAROUND (packaging hygiene; arguably upstreamable to
         LocalSend, but it belongs in package:jni, which should not build on
         desktop Linux unless asked to).
Applies: localsend v1.18.2 (patch -p1 from the repository root).
Fixes:   jni 1.0.3 (transitive, via path_provider_android 2.3.1) is declared
         as a Linux ffiPlugin, so generated_plugins.cmake always
         add_subdirectory()s it. Its src/CMakeLists.txt does a non-REQUIRED
         find_package(JNI COMPONENTS JVM); when the build host has a JDK
         (this one has jdk-openjdk 26 installed, and bq's bwrap binds / from
         the host) it builds libdartjni.so with NEEDED libjvm.so and RUNPATH
         /usr/lib/jvm/default/lib/server, and that lands in bundle/lib.
         Nothing on Linux loads it. Measured with a CMake harness:
         without this line libdartjni.so is built and linked to libjvm.so;
         with it, jni_bundled_libraries is empty.
---
diff --git a/app/linux/CMakeLists.txt b/app/linux/CMakeLists.txt
index 857775b..caca68b 100644
--- a/app/linux/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/app/linux/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -87,6 +87,12 @@ set_target_properties(${BINARY_NAME}
   RUNTIME_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY "${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/intermediates_do_not_run"
 )
 
+# The `jni` FFI plugin (pulled in by path_provider_android) is Android-only in
+# practice, but on Linux it builds libdartjni.so linked against libjvm.so,
+# with a RUNPATH into /usr/lib/jvm, whenever the build host has a JDK. Keep
+# that out of the bundle.
+set(CMAKE_DISABLE_FIND_PACKAGE_JNI TRUE)
+
 # Generated plugin build rules, which manage building the plugins and adding
 # them to the application.
 include(flutter/generated_plugins.cmake)
